{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"Federal labs are still buying one-year sole-source service on NovaSeq 6000s in Aug 2026 and for the whole of 2027, with no sign of retirement.","detail":"NCI posted notice 75N98026Q01014 on 14 Aug 2026 (due 24 Aug) for preventive maintenance on one government-owned NovaSeq 6000, S/N A01064, under FAR 6.302-1 (only one responsible source). The Naval Medical Research Command notice N3239826Q4072 (posted 22 Dec 2025) buys a one-year Silver Support Plan (CAT# 20019988, four line items of qty 1) for S/N A01716. Its response date is 31 Dec 2026. Neither notice states a dollar value. A one-year plan bought late in 2025 covers a 6000 into late 2026 or early 2027.","url":"https://govcontractfinder.com/contracts/maintenance-agreement-for-novaseq-6000-sequencing-system-75n98026q01014","date":"2026-08-14","source_name":"GovContractFinder (mirror of SAM.gov, NIH OLAO)","source_type":"procurement","quote":"only one responsible source","strength":"weak","why_new":"Dated Aug 2026 federal 6000 service notices (NCI A01064; Navy A01716) are not in the known list, which has only a Georgia core, NIEHS/NICHD, and Salk-style items."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"NCI's Frederick lab was running a NovaSeq 6000 on the premium Gold plan for Jan 2026–Jan 2027 and also adding a NovaSeq X Plus.","detail":"Solicitation M26-159 (contract 75N91019D00024, proposals due 1 Dec 2025) covers 1/21/26–1/20/27. It lists a NovaSeq 6000 (A01063) on a Gold Support Plan, a NovaSeq X Plus (LH00551) on a NovaSeq X Plus Silver plan, a NextSeq X Plus, a MiSeq, and two DRAGEN servers. This is a dual-running 6000 and X site in a federal lab, and the 6000 gets the higher service tier. A related solicitation, M25-214 (due 22 Jan 2026), covers another X Plus (LH00584), coverage 26 Mar 2026–25 Mar 2027.","url":"https://frederick.cancer.gov/work-us/vendors-subcontractors/business-opportunities/service-maintenance-agreement-illumina-lab-equipment","date":"2025-12-01","source_name":"NCI Frederick business opportunities page","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"This is a named federal dual-running 6000+X site with the service tier shown, which the known list does not have."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"Annual sole-source 6000 service renewals show the same federal sites renewing every year for several years, not decommissioning.","detail":"NIEHS bought service on its 6000 for 29 Jun 2023–28 Jun 2024 (Silver renewal), 29 Jun 2024–28 Jun 2025 (Apr 2024 notice), and 29 Jun 2025–28 Jun 2026 (switched to a Bronze plan, notice 75N96025Q00037). NICHD renewed a 6000+MiSeq Silver plan for 15 Feb 2025–14 Feb 2026. NIA/NIDA posted a 6000 maintenance synopsis on 5 Mar 2025 for 13 Apr–12 Oct 2025. NIEHS moving from Silver to Bronze means it is buying less service on the same box, so the instrument is in a low-use tail phase. This is a small sample and not a census.","url":"https://www.samdaily.us/archive/2024/04-April/05-Apr-2024/FBO-07018207.htm","date":"2025-06-13","source_name":"Loren Data SAM Daily / sweetspotgov mirror","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"The multi-year NIEHS Silver→Bronze downgrade path and the NIA 6-month term are new."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"The only 6000 service value found is $144,910 a year for a CDC 6000+MiSeq pair, so a tail box costs the customer about $100K+ a year before any reagents.","detail":"CDC solicitation 75D30125Q78540 (posted 10 Oct 2024, due 21 Oct) is a sole-source, firm-fixed-price contract for NovaSeq 6000 and MiSeq maintenance, 7 Dec 2024–6 Dec 2025, estimated at $144,910.12. If MiSeq is about $15–25K, the 6000 is about $120–130K a year. For scale, the known NHRI service was about $110K per unit per year. Against Illumina's FY26 guide of $600–650K pull-through per 6000, service of about $125K is about 20% of reagent spend for a typical box. For a low-volume 6000 using only a few flow cells a year, the fixed service fee makes the box far more expensive per Gb. That is a push to convert.","url":"https://console.sweetspotgov.com/federal-contracts/3fe396bd-4010-5305-b055-174a2bb9bf3b","date":"2024-10-10","source_name":"CDC Office of Acquisition Services via sweetspotgov","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"medium","why_new":"This is a hard dollar value for U.S. 6000 service. The known list has only NHRI Taiwan, Brazil and a $145K federal public-health lab contract in the leads."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"against","claim":"The 6000 service notice count is small and flat, and the notices are mostly tied to single government-owned boxes, so they do not show a growing tail.","detail":"I found about 8 dated US 6000-related service notices: 2024: NIEHS (Apr), CDC (Oct). 2025: NICHD (coverage from Feb), NIA (Mar), NIEHS Bronze (Jun), Navy (Dec), Frederick M26-159 (Dec 2025 deadline). 2026: NCI A01064 (Aug). That is about 2 in 2024, 4–5 in 2025 and 1–2 so far in 2026. Mirror sites are incomplete and SAM.gov could not be opened, so no trend can be claimed. Also, every notice is a one-year renewal, which means agencies could stop buying at any anniversary.","url":"https://govcontractfinder.com/contracts/comprehensive-full-service-maintenance-repair-plan-for-illum-N3239826Q4072","date":"2025-12-22","source_name":"GovContractFinder / SAM Daily / sweetspotgov","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"This is the first notice count by year; it shows no acceleration of federal 6000 service demand."},
{"label":"1A","direction":"supports","claim":"Service on resold or retiring 6000s cannot be bought from third parties, because every federal notice cites Illumina as the sole source.","detail":"All notices cite FAR 6.302-1 or FAR 13.106-1(b)(1) 'only one responsible source' and Illumina-certified technicians. Even the Navy notice, flagged 'Full & Open Competition', says it is sole source to Illumina. This leaves Illumina holding the service stream on every 6000 until it issues an end-of-life notice.","url":"https://console.sweetspotgov.com/federal-contracts/3f2f007c-f39c-5beb-8cb4-586a6eafd310","date":"2025-06-13","source_name":"sweetspotgov (NIEHS notice mirror)","source_type":"procurement","quote":"","strength":"weak","why_new":"It adds federal-notice confirmation, though similar points are in the known list (F899, F900)."},
